  "preamble": "Replacement of the alveolar trill [r] by the uvular [ʁ], the European 'guttural R'. Northern French replaced the alveolar trill with a uvular trill from the end of the 17th century, and Parisian French then weakened it to a fricative or approximant. In European Portuguese the uvular realization of the trill spread from upper-class Lisbon in the 19th century to most urban areas.",
